 leo:{persona:'A beach football regular who tries little skills, then uses them to help the team.',lines:['A skill is only fancy if it helps the team. A simple pass can be the best trick.','Sand teaches soft feet. Try keeping the ball close here, then on grass.']},
 amina:{persona:'A team captain who leads by including everyone.',lines:['A captain’s armband is just cloth. Leading is what you do for others.','Before a game I make sure everyone knows their job and feels welcome.']},
 diego:{persona:'A tactics fan who sketches formations in a notebook after every game.',lines:['Every formation has gaps. Good teams move together to cover them.','Draw three dots and connect them: that’s a passing triangle.']},
 jules:{persona:'A winger who loves sunset training by the water and well-timed runs.',lines:['A good run is about timing. Wait, then go!','From the dock you can see the ferry. Finish your paths and ride it to the final!']},
 nico:{persona:'A defender who helps at the market and enjoys stopping attacks.',lines:['Defending is patience. Wait for the loose touch, then win the ball.','Winning the ball is half the job. The next pass starts the attack.']},
 imani:{persona:'A scores reporter who reads every match beyond the scoreline.',lines:['A 1–0 can be thrilling and a 4–3 can be messy. Watch how the goals happened.','I always check the source and date before I share a score.']},
 rafi:{persona:'A transfer news enthusiast who keeps rumours separate from confirmed moves.',lines:['A rumour is not a signing until the club announces it.','The best signings fit how a team plays, not just a famous name.']},
 mei:{persona:'A community organiser who makes sure every newcomer gets a game.',lines:['Fair teams make fun games. Mix them up if one side is winning by lots.','Got only three friends? Play two against one and swap often.']},
 luz:{persona:'A community gardener who treats gardens and teams the same way: with shared care.',lines:['Gardens and teams grow the same way: a little care from everyone, every day.','Fresh vegetables help you grow strong for football.']},
 ben:{persona:'A courtyard volunteer who sweeps up, then plays.',lines:['Leave a space better than you found it. That goes for pitches too.','Respect the rules, respect the players, respect the place.']},
 ines:{persona:'A café worker whose shift ends with a friendly team game.',lines:['Our café team has cooks, servers and a dishwasher who is a brilliant keeper.','Half-time is for one clear idea, not ten!']},
 ada:{persona:'A garden volunteer practising patience with her weaker foot.',lines:['My weaker foot is like a seedling: water it every day and it grows.','Ten passes with your weaker foot each day adds up fast.']},
 omar:{persona:'A garden keeper who plays in goal on match days.',lines:['A bouncing ball is tricky. Watch it all the way into your hands.','Seedlings and goalkeepers both need patience.']},
